> \]”

whose residue is \(\eta^{-\lfloor\ell_1u/e_1\rfloor}\). No displayed hypothesis identifies \(z_1=\eta\).

Counter-configuration: take \(K_1=\mathbf F_3\), \(e_1=2,f_1=h=1\), \(\eta=2\), \(\ell_1=1\), and \(u_2=3\). The computed quotient has residue \(\eta^{-1}=2\). Because the carrier leaves \(z_1\) unconstrained, assigning \(z_1=1\) makes (C1-level-2) predict residue \(1\).

FINDING G2 — GAP: normalized cocycle identities require an unstated zero-height normalization.

Verbatim:

> “At a general level \(i\), fix exact-height normalizers \(\widehat n_i(m)\)…”

followed by

> “\[
